- Forgot → `sendPasswordResetEmail` → clear confirmation notice
- Set New Password (`PasswordRecoveryHost`) when `PASSWORD_RECOVERY` fires → `updatePassword`

## Backend — Supabase (LOCKED — V1)

### Client
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` + `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- AsyncStorage session persistence via `lib/supabase.js`

### `public.profiles` (RLS enabled)
- `id uuid primary key references auth.users (id) on delete cascade`
- `username`, `real_name`, `age`, `gender`, `email`, `phone`, `country`, `category`, `role`, `created_at`

### Auth & persistence flow
- Create Account → `signUpWithEmailPassword` → `supabase.auth.signUp({ email, password, options: { data: { phone } } })`
- Sign In → `signInWithEmailPassword` → `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password })`
- Forgot → `sendPasswordResetEmail` → `supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(email)`
- Set new → `updatePassword` → `supabase.auth.updateUser({ password })`
- Then `upsertRegisteredProfile` with V1 form fields keyed by auth user id
- Soft-fail if offline / schema mismatch — still complete local registration / enter Arena
- **Never re-add** SMS OTP as the primary auth path

## App wiring

- Entry mounts `AthleteRegistrationScreen` from `App.js` (not a parallel LandingScreen).
- Logout → `loginOnly: true` Email + Password Sign In screen.
- `PasswordRecoveryHost` mounted in `App.js` beside invite host.
- Do not strip `flag` / `country` / `location` / `gender` / `age` / `username` / `category` / `phone` / `email` from the session payload.

## Allowed elsewhere

- New features outside this stack. Crash/security fixes that must touch these files: ask first; preserve this contract.
